{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "5f2bdf9f-a4e9-8fee-8349-75369556876d",
  "created_at": "2026-03-05T12:06:30-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, City Clerk",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Carmen Salazar",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Owen Haskell",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:03:59-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Clerk's office, this is Owen. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:04:03-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, honey. Oh, good, a real person. I was afraid I'd get one of those menus. Um, my name is Carmen Salazar, and I think I need a marriage license, but I'm honestly not sure how it works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:04:15-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can help with that. Who is the license for, if you don't mind my asking?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:04:21-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, it's for my niece and her fella. I manage a few rentals, so everybody calls me when there's paperwork. She asked me to find out, and I said, Carmen will call. Now, do I come in, or does she? I thought maybe I could just pick it up for her."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:04:37-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both people getting married need to come in together, in person. One person can't pick it up for the couple."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:04:44-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both of them. Okay. Dear, so what do they bring? Is it a birth certificate? I thought it was the baptism paper, but maybe that's the church."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:04:53-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The church paper is separate. They'd bring a photo ID each. If either has been married before, they should bring the details of how that ended, the date and so on. I'd suggest calling back with their situation so I can confirm the rest."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:05:07-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wait, so the ID is for the license, and the other thing is for the church. Did I say that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:05:14-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Close. The ID is for the license. The church has its own requirements, and you'd ask them about those."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:05:21-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. And how long does it take? Do they walk out with it that day, or do we wait? Because the wedding is soon and I get nervous. We have three generations living in one house, so it's a lot of people to organize, and everybody has an opinion."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:05:37-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. I'd tell them to come in well ahead of the wedding date. Often it can be done at the counter the same visit, but I'd confirm that when they come, since I don't want you planning around the wrong thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:05:51-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So same day, maybe. But maybe not. Now I'm a little mixed up, honey. Is it the license that takes time, or the certificate after the wedding?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:06:00-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Those are two different things. The license is what they get before the wedding. The certificate is the record afterward. Today we're only talking about the license."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:06:09-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, the license first. Okay. I'll write that down. License, both of them, ID. And I'll tell her to call you about the other part."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:06:17-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That works. We're open weekdays, and she can ask for me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:06:21-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, dear. You were very patient. I'll try to get it straight for her."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T12:06:27-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Anytime. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
